# core/coverage-gaps - Which elements of this type lack an expected property?
#
# Answers: elements of RESOURCE_TYPE with no EXPECTED_PREDICATE asserted.
#
# Does NOT prove: that the real thing lacks the property. It proves nobody
# recorded it. "No owner is modelled" and "this system has no owner" are different
# statements, and reporting the second when you measured the first is the most
# damaging mistake available here.
#
# Before reporting a gap, check three things. That RESOURCE_TYPE actually has
# instances - a type with zero members produces zero gaps and looks like perfect
# coverage. That the predicate spelling is right - use core/element-detail on one
# element you know carries it. And which models are in scope, since a gap
# concentrated in one model is usually a partial export, not an ownership problem.
#
# Parameters: RESOURCE_TYPE, EXPECTED_PREDICATE, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT ?element ?label ?model
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    ?element a {{RESOURCE_TYPE}} .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?element {{EXPECTED_PREDICATE}} ?anyValue }
    OPTIONAL { ?element {{PATH:label}} ?label }
    OPTIONAL { ?element {{ROLE:part_of}} ?model }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY ?model ?label ?element
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
